{"fetch_error_details function lacks explicit timeout handling and could amplify latency issues if nodestore is slow - needs timeout parameter with reasonable default (e.g., 500ms)": 0.22286708652973175, "fetch_error_details should implement graceful degradation to continue with breadcrumbs-only if the fetch fails or times out": 0.22379979491233826, "fetch_error_details missing metrics to track fetch latency and failure rates to detect nodestore performance issues": 0.09839778393507004, "Chronological merge assumes consistent timestamp semantics between error events and replay breadcrumbs - if systems use different time sources or precision, ordering may be incorrect": 0.09777044504880905, "Chronological merge needs deterministic tie-breaking logic (e.g., by event type or ID) when timestamps are equal": 0.0458587221801281, "Chronological merge should validate that timestamps are in a comparable format/timezone": 0.07682812213897705, "fromJSON() method now returns Visualize[] instead of single Visualize instance - breaking API change that will break code expecting single object": 0.7874754071235657, "Asymmetric compatibility where toJSON maintains legacy shape but fromJSON changes contract creates migration risk for persisted visualizations, URL parameters, and downstream consumers": 0.5860626697540283, "Changing from yAxes: readonly string[] to yAxis: string is breaking internal API change affecting ~20 files with risk for less-tested code paths and persisted query state": 0.5849014520645142, "Missing contract tests for round-trip serialization with both old and new payload formats to ensure compatibility": 0.1434156596660614, "Owner field update logic should enforce mutual exclusivity between owner_user_id and owner_team_id at model level, not just serializer - possible to end up with both fields set during concurrent updates": 0.22570455074310303, "Mutual exclusivity validation between age and timestamp checks self.initial_data in field validator, causing order-dependent validation behavior - should use validate() method for object-level validation": 0.4080592691898346, "isVisualize type guard changed to check for single yAxis string instead of yAxes array - objects with old shape will fail guard and be incorrectly classified if persisted state contains old format": 0.7283274531364441, "Logic change from map to flatMap combined with Visualize.fromJSON() returning array could lead to unexpected URL parameter multiplication and URL bloat": 0.29172375798225403}